  "body": "**Blocked by:** #118\n\n## Context\n\nProcess memory is disposable, while long conversations can exceed the model context before their next turn.\n\n## Task\n\nReconstruct dormant delegated and Semp conversations from the complete ordered `agent_run_events` history into `initialState.messages`. Before the first resumed turn, call public `estimateContextTokens(messages)` and `shouldCompact(tokens,contextWindow,settings)`. When required, convert stored events to the exact `Entry[]` tree (`id`, `parentId`, `seq`, `timestamp`, `message`) and use public low-level `prepareCompaction` plus `compact`; do not call the unfinished `AgentLane.compact()` wrapper or pi internals. Persist the resulting valid continuation/audit events so repeated restart remains deterministic.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Reconstruction, protocol validation, pre-turn sizing, low-level compaction, and restart tests.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Custom compaction algorithms and unexported pi modules.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A restarted conversation resumes with prior context.\n- Oversized history compacts before provider invocation.\n- Tool-use/result invariants remain valid after reconstruction.\n",
